{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgfhdod5HT23UuZMZ4fy7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Dq ≈ 1470 cm⁻¹; B cannot be determined from this spectrum.**\n\n**Why B is not accessible.** For a d⁹ ion, the ground state is ²E_g (octahedral) or ²B₁g (tetragonal), and the excited states are ²T₂g or the tetragonal ²B₂g/²E_g/²A₁g. Because d⁹ is a single positive hole in a d shell, its one-electron-hole d–d energies depend only on Dq and the tetragonal splitting parameters. The Racah B (and C) terms cancel out of the transition energies. The band positions therefore carry no information about B, so B is not determinable from this data.\n\n**Why Dq is only approximate.** In O_h, the single spin-allowed d–d band for d⁹ is ²E_g → ²T₂g, at 10Dq. The complex is tetragonally distorted (axial aqua ligands, Jahn–Teller), so the band splits into components. The broad band at 14 720 cm⁻¹ is taken as the dominant component, giving:\n\n10Dq ≈ 14 720 cm⁻¹ → Dq ≈ 1472 cm⁻¹ ≈ 1470 cm⁻¹\n\nThe shoulder at 12 240 cm⁻¹ is probably a lower tetragonal component. Using the band centre instead (≈13 480 cm⁻¹) would give Dq ≈ 1350 cm⁻¹, so the value carries roughly ±10% uncertainty from the band assignment.\n\nThe C parameter is likewise undetermined here.\n\n{\"Dq\": 1470, \"B\": null, \"C\": null, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Dq estimated from the d9 band maximum (10Dq), but B cannot be determined because d9 transition energies do not depend on the Racah parameters.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":218,"cache_read_input_tokens":1480,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":218,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":